course: dictionary
lesson: 14606
title: Polka
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A polka is a lively, bouncy dance for two people, with quick hopping steps. It began in Central Europe in the 1800s. Its music has two beats in each bar, so it sounds fast and cheerful.
explain: Read the words around the word to find its meaning. «The band struck up a polka, and the whole village hopped onto the dance floor.» Band, dance floor and hopping are the clues. A polka must be a fast dance that people do together.
explain: Polka also means a pattern. «Her blue cup had white polka dots.» Here there are no dancers. The dots are round, all the same size, and spread evenly over the cup. Ask yourself: which meaning fits the sentence?
fact: A polka is a fast, happy dance for couples, with quick hopping steps.
fact: The polka started in Central Europe in the 1800s.
fact: The music for a polka usually has two beats in a bar.
fact: «Polka dots» are round dots of the same size, spread evenly over cloth.
fact: To check the meaning, swap it into the sentence and see if it still makes sense.
exercise: «The whole class danced a polka at the school party.» What is a polka? | *A lively dance for couples with quick hopping steps | A type of cake | A slow, sleepy lullaby
exercise: «Her new dress had red polka dots.» What are polka dots? | Long stripes running down the cloth | *Round dots of the same size, spread evenly over cloth | Small pictures of animals
exercise: «Mum played polka music on the radio while we cooked.» What kind of music is it likely to be? | *Fast music with two beats in a bar | Music sung by a choir of birds | Slow music for falling asleep | Music with no beat at all
test: «The polka is danced by couples who hop quickly across the floor.» Who dances a polka? | *Couples | Sleeping babies | Single runners on a track | Penguins in a line
test: «The village held a party, and the band played a polka all night.» What does the polka tell the reader? | A school exam is starting | A storm is coming | *There is a cheerful party or dance | Someone is lost in the woods
exam: Ayesha says «polka dots» are a fast dance. Is she right? | No, polka dots are a type of fish | Yes, polka dots are a kind of music played on drums | Yes, polka dots are a fast dance for couples | *No, polka dots are round, evenly spaced spots on cloth
